Here is the exact terminal setup script to install every required tool on your Ubuntu system, fully configured to support your testing workflow.
------------------------------
## 🛠️ Section 1: Standard System Utilities
Open your Ubuntu terminal and run the following command block to update your system packages and install basic development requirements, Git, and Java (which is needed to run Burp Suite).

sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y
sudo apt install -y curl git default-jdk build-essential libimage-exiftool-perl python3 python3-pip python3-venv

------------------------------
## 💻 Section 2: Go Language Runtime Installation
Many modern testing tools require Go. Run these commands sequentially to download, install, and configure Go on your system.

# Download the Go binary archive
curl -OL https://go.dev
# Extract it to your system directory
sudo tar -C /usr/local -xzf go1.22.2.linux-amd64.tar.gz
# Clean up the downloaded file
rm go1.22.2.linux-amd64.tar.gz
# Append Go environment paths to your shell profile
echo 'export PATH=$PATH:/usr/local/go/bin' >> ~/.bashrc
echo 'export PATH=$PATH:$HOME/go/bin' >> ~/.bashrc
# Reload your shell configurations
source ~/.bashrc

