## 🔍 Section 3: Tool-Specific Setup Instructions## 1. Burp Suite Community Edition (Area 1, 2, 3, & 4)
Ubuntu provides a straightforward automated installer script for Burp Suite.

# Download the official Linux installer script
curl -o burpsuite_community.sh "https://portswigger-cdn.net"
# Grant execution permissions
chmod +x burpsuite_community.sh
# Execute the installer wizard
./burpsuite_community.sh


* Post-Installation Step (Extensions): Open Burp Suite → Navigate to Extensions tab → Click BApp Store → Search for and install Autorize and Turbo Intruder.

## 2. Interactsh Client (Area 3 & 4)
This manages out-of-band interaction logging for your SSRF and Blind XSS tests.

# Install the binary using Go
go install -v ://github.com

## 3. OWASP ZAP (Area 2 Alternate)
If you want to use ZAP instead of Burp for breakpoints, install the official community snap package.

sudo snap install owasp-zap --classic

## 4. CyberChef Offline Edition (Area 2)
Running CyberChef locally on Ubuntu keeps your cryptographic testing private and efficient.

# Create a dedicated directory
mkdir -p ~/tools/cyberchef && cd ~/tools/cyberchef
# Pull down the latest standalone package structure
curl -OL https://github.com
# Install unzip utility and extract packages
sudo apt install unzip -y
unzip CyberChef_v10.19.4.zip
# Open the HTML application in your default Ubuntu browser
xdg-open CyberChef_v10.19.4.html

## 5. Exiftool (Area 4 Image Modification)
Exiftool was successfully installed via the system package command in Section 1. You can instantly run and verify its deployment in your terminal workspace:

exiftool -ver

